ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(396.8,-345) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"39\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-39\"></use><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"1260.7\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3612,0)\"><use data-c=\"3C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(4667.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.\n<br>So we can say in M mixture of M<sup>+2</sup> and M<sup>+3</sup> present.\n<br><br>Assume total no of atoms present in M is 100.\n<br>Let M<sup>+3</sup> present in M = y atoms\n<br>So M<sup>+2</sup> present in M = (100 - y) atoms\n<br><br>In 1 atom of M<sup>+3</sup> charge present = +3\n<br>So in y atoms of M<sup>+3</sup> charge present = +3y\n<br><br>Similarly in 1 atom of M<sup>+2</sup> charge present = +2\n<br>So in (100 - y) atoms of M<sup>+2</sup> charge present = +2(100 - y)\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Total charge = 200 - 2y + 3y = 200 + y\n<br><br>In 100 atoms of M total charge = 200 + y\n<br>So in 1 ato